      "level": 1,
      "content": "SQL AND Operator"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The AND operator is used in the WHERE clause to combine multiple conditions where all conditions must be TRUE for a row to be included in the results."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Consider the previous example where you want to find customers between the ages of 23 and 27."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This requires two conditions to be TRUE:"
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet_list",
      "items": [
        "The customer's age must be greater than or equal to 23.",
        "The customer's age must be less than or equal to 27."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here's how you can combine these conditions using the AND operator:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "sql",
      "content": "1-- Select rows where age is between 23 and 27\n2\n3SELECT first_name, age  \n4FROM Customers  \n5WHERE age >= 23 AND age <= 27;"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here's how this query works:"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Working of the AND operator",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The AND operator ensures that both conditions (age >= 23 and age <= 27) must be TRUE for a row to appear in the results."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "How does it work?"
